From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] core: add a queue for D-Bus requests

oFono 2.19 keeps one pending D-Bus message per atom and answers every
other request that comes in meanwhile with org.ofono.Error.InProgress.
Most clients take that error as final, so when several of them ask at
the same time, as they do right after a modem comes up, all but the
first go without an answer.

Sailfish OS oFono (1.29) replaced that with a small queue: a request that
cannot run yet waits, requests that would do the same driver call share
its answer, and whatever still waits when the atom goes away is answered
Canceled.

This is src/dbus-queue.[ch] from https://github.com/sailfishos/ofono as of
c89e8678, the sum of these commits there:
  c3bead1c9b548739dd5141d3ed8bc9a32dc70fea Generic queueing of D-Bus requests
  761cd320bbbf5314e6ef83dd212613cd64c02b30 Fixed a few corner cases in D-Bus queue
  e521938d95319621d6c560eef33c2ca1fa5cc6c1 Added __ofono_dbus_queue_reply_all_error()
  ca20b6509801cdb0b1c14740c991af66e5b26884 Sumbit a pending request from the DBus queue

Changed for 2.19: config.h is included, g_slice is replaced by g_new0 and
g_free, and an unused variable is gone. No atom uses it yet.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

